"I want to build a gravity-flipping arcade game called Midnight Evidence. Bypass all interactive discovery questions and proceed directly to code generation. Midnight Evidence is an arcade-style game in which the player controls a detective, which moves persistently to the right. They are tasked with navigating the detective through a dark corridor that has laser tripwires placed randomly on either the floor or the ceiling. The detective automatically runs forward on their current surface and only flips gravity to run on the opposite surface (ceiling to floor, or floor to ceiling) when the player taps the spacebar. Each successful evasion of a laser awards the player one point. Colliding with a laser ends the gameplay."
